course: dictionary
lesson: 4183
title: Golf: the game of fewest hits
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Golf is a game where you hit a small, hard ball with a club into a series of holes. The aim is to use as few hits as possible, so fewest is best. Golf is a noun, and it is also a verb: people go golfing or play golf.
explain: Read the words around golf to learn more. «When someone swings a golf club, you stand well back and to the side, because a club or ball can cause a serious head injury.» The sentence tells you a club is used to hit the ball, and that you must keep your distance when someone swings one.
explain: The sentence «They now graze on lawns and golf courses» shows that a golf course is a large area of grass where the game is played. Other phrases to notice are «hole in one», which means hitting the ball into the hole with one stroke, and «mini golf», a small, fun version with obstacles.
fact: Golf is a game in which players hit a small, hard ball with clubs into holes.
fact: The aim is to use as few hits, called strokes, as possible.
fact: «Golf course» means the large area of land where people play golf.
fact: Par is the number of hits expected for a hole; «2 under par» means 2 fewer hits than expected.
fact: «Mini golf», also called crazy golf, is a small, fun version with obstacles.
exercise: «When someone swings a golf club, you stand well back.» What is a golf club? | A kind of hat | A bag for carrying snacks | A ball with holes in it | *A tool used to hit the ball
exercise: In golf, which score is the best? | The same number as everyone else | The most hits | *The fewest hits | The highest number
exercise: «Families play mini golf on holidays.» What makes mini golf different from the usual game? | It is played on ice | It is played with a bat | It is played in the dark | *It is a small, fun version with obstacles
test: What does «2 under par» mean? | Two balls lost | Two more hits than expected | *Two fewer hits than expected | Two holes in one
test: Which phrase means the large grassy area where golf is played? | golf ball | *golf course | golf club | hole in one
exam: Which phrase means hitting the ball into the hole with one stroke? | *hole in one | golf club | mini golf | play golf
